rst Lombard Duke of Trent, named by Paul the Deacon, ruling from around 569 or 575 until his death in 595.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/eulalia-of-merida"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/eulalia-of-merida.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Eulalia of Mérida</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Eulalia of Mérida was a young Christian martyred at Emerita Augusta, capital of Roman Lusitania, in 304 during the persecution of Diocletian.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/eulji-mundeok"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/eulji-mundeok.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Eulji Mundeok</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Eulji Mundeok was a Goguryeo general who led the defence against the invasion of Emperor Yang of Sui in 612.</span></a></li></ul>
